You can catch exceptions (errors) in python with the try except else and finally methods.

try: Something that might cause an exceptions
except: Do this if there is an exception
else: Do this if there were no exceptions
finally: Do this no matter what happens

You can have multiple excepts to catch multiple errors and do different things with each

except KeyError as error_message: stores the error value inside error_message

You can raise your own value errors

